<title>SWITZERLAND: Ciba H1 net profit rises 6.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Ciba H1 net profit rises 6.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     1,596	     vs  1,502</p>
<p> Group operating profit     2,191	     vs  2,135</p>
<p> Sales			    11,428	    vs  10,952</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit		 2,115	     vs 2,019</p>
<p> Taxes			    519		 vs 517</p>
<p> Cost of sales		  5,245	     vs 4,981</p>
<p> Gross profit		   6,183	     vs 5,971</p>
<p> Marketing &amp; distribution   1,770	     vs 1,704</p>
<p> Research &amp; development     972		 vs 925</p>
<p> General, administration    1,250	     vs 1,207</p>
<p> Total expenses		 3,992	     vs 3,836</p>
<p> Net financial result	 76 loss	   vs 116 loss</p>
<p> Financial income	     143		 vs 200</p>
<p> Financial expense	    238		 vs 241</p>
<p> Currency gains		 26		  vs 68 loss</p>
<p> Minority interests	   7		   vs 7</p>
<p> Total assets		   33,149	    vs 29,652</p>
<p> Cash at end-June	     7,634	     vs 6,624</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Swiss pharmaceuticals group is Ciba-Geigy AG. Analysts on average had forecast a net profit rise of 11.3 percent to 1.67 billion francs with forecasts ranging from 10 to 13 percent.  </p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
